Looking at this large PR, which is primarily a mechanical move of database migrations from `packages/cli` to `packages/@n8n/db` with import path updates.

Let me focus on the substantive changes rather than the mechanical renames.

```json
{
  "comments": [
    {
      "path": "packages/@n8n/db/src/migrations/migration-helpers.ts",
      "start_line": 45,
      "end_line": 45,
      "content": "Replacing `inTest` (from `@n8n/backend-common`) with `process.env.NODE_ENV === 'test'` subtly changes behavior. The `inTest` helper typically also accounts for `NODE_ENV === 'e2e'` (or other test-detection logic) and can be centrally toggled. This raw env check may cause migration start/end logs to be emitted in test contexts that were previously suppressed (and vice versa). Consider exposing a small test-detection utility in `@n8n/constants`/`@n8n/config` instead of duplicating the raw env check, to keep parity with the original behavior."
    },
    {
      "path": "packages/@n8n/db/src/migrations/common/1724951148974-AddApiKeysTable.ts",
      "start_line": 42,
      "end_line": 42,
      "content": "The added `// @ts-expect-error Tech debt` suppresses a real typing mismatch on the map callback. Since `runQuery` results are untyped here, prefer typing the array (e.g. `usersWithApiKeys: Array<{ id: string; apiKey: string }>`) at its declaration rather than suppressing per-callback, so the suppression doesn't mask future genuine type errors in this block."
    }
  ]
}
